    <help format="markdown"><![CDATA[
## What it does

Evaluates one Kraken recognition model against transcribed test data using
`ketos test`. Use held-out data that was not used for training or model selection
when estimating recognition quality.

## Inputs

- Model weights from Ketos Train (Safetensors or CoreML), or a training checkpoint.
- One or more Arrow datasets produced by Ketos Compile; or image/ground-truth
  pairs in line/transcription, ALTO, or PAGE XML format.

Pairs can be selected individually or supplied as a `list:paired` collection.
The forward element is the image; the reverse element is the transcription or
XML annotation. Each XML annotation must describe its paired image. The tool
updates the image reference for the job. Multi-page TIFF images must be split
into single-page images first.

## Output and options

The text output contains Kraken's evaluation log and accuracy report, including
character accuracy, case-insensitive character accuracy, word accuracy,
insertions, deletions, substitutions, and character confusions.

Architecture is detected from the model by default. Match text direction and
normalization to the conventions used for your ground truth. Optional batch
size, padding, and line type override Kraken's defaults. Legacy polygon
extraction follows the model unless explicitly disabled.

Kraken is licensed under the Apache-2.0 license.
    ]]></help>
